# .worktreeinclude: gitignored files Claude Code copies into every worktree it
# creates (`claude --worktree`, subagent worktrees, desktop parallel sessions).
# Syntax: `.gitignore` patterns, one per line. Only files that match a pattern and
# are gitignored are copied, so tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# Never list `.env` files, `secrets/` or key files here, even though the vendor's
# example does: a worktree per agent multiplies every secret it copies. Give each
# worktree its credentials through the environment or a secret manager instead.
# `doctor` reports a `.worktreeinclude` that lists one of them.
#
# List the local, non-secret files a fresh checkout needs to build and test, such as
# a generated local configuration. This file is the project's: the installer seeds
# it once and never rewrites it.
